    "type": "question",
    "label": "2",
    "prompt": "Find rational $a$ and $b$ such that\n$$\\left(1+\\sqrt{2}\\right)^4=a+b\\sqrt{2}.$$",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$a=17,\\quad b=12$",
      "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}(1+\\sqrt{2})^4&=1+4\\sqrt{2}+6(\\sqrt{2})^2+4(\\sqrt{2})^3+(\\sqrt{2})^4\\\\(1+\\sqrt{2})^4&=1+4\\sqrt{2}+12+8\\sqrt{2}+4\\\\(1+\\sqrt{2})^4&=17+12\\sqrt{2}\\end{align*}$$\n\nComparing rational and surd terms gives $a=17$ and $b=12$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
